      "published": "2026-11-15T16:04:01Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Current USCO precedent denies copyright to machine output, placing purely AI-generated code functionally into the public domain.",
        "Models trained on open-source code risk GPL license-laundering unless synthesized outputs carry mandatory permissive or copyleft disclosure terms.",
        "Mandating open access for generated code improves supply-chain auditability, letting engineering teams systematically scan synthetic dependencies for security defects."
      ]
    },
